(7481313, 1189683, 67688, '<td valign="top">What a well deserved winner.. well spotted Anita!</td>', 'What a well deserved winner.. well spotted Anita!', '2016-11-07 03:36:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481316, 1189597, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Your high vantage point has enabled you to add interest by illustrating how precarious a simple task like cleaning windows can be when faced with a high-rise block. In choosing to do so you have made the building dominate the image and whilst the left wall is interesting this face is rather dull and has the effect of reducing the overall impact. Given that the left of the image is much more dynamic a more effective option would have been to compose the image with the end wall on the right and the cityscape in the rest of the frame still fulfilling the challenge brief. Thanks for your entry Marcel</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge Your high vantage point has enabled you to add interest by illustrating how precarious a simple task like cleaning windows can be when faced with a high-rise block. In choosing to do so you have made the building dominate the image and whilst the left wall is interesting this face is rather dull and has the effect of reducing the overall impact. Given that the left of the image is much more dynamic a more effective option would have been to compose the image with the end wall on the right and the cityscape in the rest of the frame still fulfilling the challenge brief. Thanks for your entry Marcel', '2016-11-07 06:34:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481318, 1189763, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge fully<br/> <br/>Regardless of the opinion of one of your commenters this still remains a classic image for good reason. Technically it is up to your normal high standards though I do agree with Neat, the greens, reds and bright yellow are very dominant in a near mono cityscape. Your title reflects the current heightened tensions of the continuing terrorist threat that France in particular is enduring. A very worthy score and result for a very worthy image, well done Janine.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge fully Regardless of the opinion of one of your commenters this still remains a classic image for good reason. Technically it is up to your normal high standards though I do agree with Neat, the greens, reds and bright yellow are very dominant in a near mono cityscape. Your title reflects the current heightened tensions of the continuing terrorist threat that France in particular is enduring. A very worthy score and result for a very worthy image, well done Janine.', '2016-11-07 06:48:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481319, 1189874, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge fully<br/> <br/>A lovely atmospheric landscape that works even better with the mono conversion. Well done for exercising patience and waiting for the break in the weather to include the village which not only adds interest but also a sense of scale to this grand scene. You have a nice range of tones throughout, all in all a very pleasing image, well done Jonathon</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge fully A lovely atmospheric landscape that works even better with the mono conversion. Well done for exercising patience and waiting for the break in the weather to include the village which not only adds interest but also a sense of scale to this grand scene. You have a nice range of tones throughout, all in all a very pleasing image, well done Jonathon', '2016-11-07 06:53:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481320, 1189459, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge fully<br/> <br/>An interesting write-up of the difficulties posed using the lens that you were, a sensible and effective way round the problem. I dont see the perceived slant on the bridge as a problem at all it is perfectly reasonable to expect to see such a result in real life. If you can get back there to repeat the shot I suspect this will be looking glorious now with more of its autumnal colours add to the golden glow of that lovely bridge. A lot of your images, this included, bring back fond memories from my canal boating days, thanks Eugene.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge fully An interesting write-up of the difficulties posed using the lens that you were, a sensible and effective way round the problem. I dont see the perceived slant on the bridge as a problem at all it is perfectly reasonable to expect to see such a result in real life. If you can get back there to repeat the shot I suspect this will be looking glorious now with more of its autumnal colours add to the golden glow of that lovely bridge. A lot of your images, this included, bring back fond memories from my canal boating days, thanks Eugene.', '2016-11-07 07:02:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481324, 1189683, 109227, '<td valign="top">Congrats Anita, simplicity and contrast at it''s best.</td>', 'Congrats Anita, simplicity and contrast at it''s best.', '2016-11-07 07:51:45.000000', NULL, 0),
